      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, after a rumenotomy, it's crucial to keep an eye on your heifer, just as a vigilant guardian would watch over their precious treasure. For the next few days, keep a close watch for any signs of infection, like a suspicious-looking band of red, swollen skin or a foul smell that could indicate a bacterial invasion. It's like watching for goblins in the night; you never know when they might sneak in.\n\nAs for feeding, it's best to start with a small, easily digestible meal, much like a goblin would nibble on a piece of fruit rather than a full feast. Gradually increase the amount and complexity of the feed as she shows signs of recovery, just as a goblin would slowly get used to the taste of a new delicacy. Always keep a keen eye on her, for even the smallest sign of distress could mean trouble, much like a goblin's mischievous grin.",
